---
import '../../styles/global.css';
import Navigation from '../../components/navbar.astro';

// Base URL for GitHub Pages
const baseUrl = '/serra2';

// Page metadata
const pageTitle = "An Iberian missprint - Serra 2.0";
const pageDescription = "Understanding the foundational principle behind Serra Angel and the Serra 2.0 project";
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <meta name="description" content={pageDescription}>
  <title>{pageTitle}</title>
</head>

<body>
  <Navigation currentPage="about" />

  <header class="page-header">
    <h1>An Iberian missprint</h1>
  </header>

  <main class="container">
    <article class="about-article">
      
      <section class="article-section">
        <p>
          This printing error of <b>Serra Angel</b> comes from the black-bordered Fourth Edition, released in Spain in 1995. 
          The Angel's illustration was replaced with that of Time Elemental, illustrated by Amy Weber. 
          It is considered one of the most famous printing errors in the history of Magic. 
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="article-image2">
        <img src=`${baseUrl}/articles/serra-angel-missprint.jpg` alt="Serra Angel missprint from the Spanish version of Fourth Edition">
      </div>

      <section class="article-section">
        <p>
          Here, the misprint becomes a work in its own right, a fragment of history and fantasy, carrying the powerful aesthetic of error. 
        </p>
      </section>

    </article>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <p>&copy; 2026 Serra 2.0 Project. All rights reserved.</p>
  </footer>
</body>
</html>